		(uuid "47e0c59a-bc23-5a13-bec3-ab2f2a55b5be")
	)
	(text "The boundary runs through U11: A-side from the digital domain, Y-side precision analogue, GND on MAGND. See floorplan.py."
		(at 254 749.3 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "ee4f6518-c7a2-5658-9d77-e60913facb03")
	)
	(text "Fail-safe: any stuck MCU state collapses the pump, the FET releases, and de-energised is bypass. D803 covers the one path the pump cannot see. See design.fail_safe()."
		(at 812.8 924.56 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "c8f32f18-8609-5d26-80bf-b71fb1c426ad")
	)
	(text "R901 is THE bond, to the mixer's TP6. R902 is internal. Constraint 2 allows exactly one of the first."
		(at 660.4 850.9 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "a56c371b-b400-5864-8618-412f006caa04")
	)
	(text "The isolation barrier runs through U15: pins 1-3 are referenced to IGND, which is the inlet's 0 V and the mixer's PGND through the shared jack; pins 6-8 to MDGND. C810 is the only other part that touches both. See design.barrier_return()."
		(at 254 1061.72 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "986409c2-c04f-5e24-975d-6346aa8a7349")
	)
	(text "The envelope ADC. AGND and DGND are one net here and both are MAGND -- DS20006181C section 7.3's second scheme, and the only one compatible with this board having exactly one analogue/digital star. Six logic signals leave for the controller and no analogue trace crosses the boundary; MCLK is one of the six because the part's own RC oscillator cannot hold 2 kHz on six channels -- see design.envelope_adc_clock()."
		(at 254 1206.5 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "7134e376-e417-512e-bde5-38f61c8731c1")
	)
	(text "The controller. Three 3.3 V and 5 V nets on this sheet and no two of them are one: V3V3 is the ADC's, linear from V5; VMOD is U22's switched 5 V, carrying the module and the relay coils; VMCU is the module's own 3.3 V, made on it by an RT6150 out of VSYS and brought back out on pin 36. V5 is what is left of the linear rail -- the reference and the ADC's LDO. U22's input is ahead of R804 so that its ripple meets the same pole the converter's own does. MINA/MINK/MINJ are on the far side of U21 and belong to whatever is sending: CA-033 forbids a DC path from them to this board's ground."
		(at 190.5 1397 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "423fc8cb-4ac7-5554-9846-de13933da2f0")
	)
